  title: >-
    Generalizable phenotype-inverse identification of compound targets from
    perturbational omics
  notes: "Manuscript submitted for publication."
  year: 2026
abstract: >-
  MeTar ranks candidate drug targets from perturbation-response data. The
  software supports bulk expression, direct and support-conditioned prediction
  in new cell lines, single-cell transcriptomics, proteomics, and consensus
  across cell lines.
keywords:
  - drug-target identification
  - perturbational omics
  - meta-learning
  - single-cell transcriptomics
  - proteomics
